# roam-340: EVERY Roamux chrome://flags row lives here — one patch for the three
# generated/flag files, collapsed from patch 0024's two flag-file sections and the
# ten per-feature *-flags-entry patches (0043, 0044, 0045, 0046, 0048, 0051, 0055,
# 0064, 0066, 0069; their numbers are retired, not reused). Before this, the same
# region of about_flags.cc was hunked by eleven patches, each carrying the earlier
# rows as context, so one upstream change there conflicted with all of them.
#
# Content is byte-identical to what the eleven patches produced (roam-340 verified
# the fully-patched tree, all 126 patched paths, equal before and after).
#
# RULES FOR THE NEXT ROW (read before adding a Roamux flag):
#   * Add it HERE, never in a per-feature patch — test_patch_inventory.py fails the
#     build if any other patch touches these three files.
#   * This patch sorts LAST among patches touching these files; keep it so.
#   * flag-metadata.json is in GLOBAL alphabetical order ("roamux-*" sorts before
#     "robust-*"/"running-*"), expiry_milestone -1 requires a
#     flag-never-expire-list.json entry, and names must be unique — enforced only
#     by AboutFlagsTest (unit_tests; NOT run by any Roamux CI job): run it locally,
#     DYLD_FRAMEWORK_PATH=roamux/third_party/sparkle out/Default/unit_tests
#     --gtest_filter='AboutFlagsTest.*'.
#   * roamux_browsertests' RoamuxFlagsEntriesTest (tier-2) asserts every expected
#     row is present, rendered and usable on chrome://flags — extend its list.
#
# Rows (11 FEATURE_VALUE_TYPE kill-switches + 1 SINGLE_VALUE_TYPE switch mirror):
#   roamux-bookmark-subfolder-groups, roamux-brave-style-profiles, roamux-edge-import,
#   roamux-external-open-profile, roamux-initial-url, roamux-new-tab-position,
#   roamux-refresh-all-initial-urls, roamux-signin-opt-in (switch; hidden by
#   ShouldSkipConditionalFeatureEntry while kBraveStyleProfiles is off),
#   roamux-tab-group-header-double-click-all (roam-322), roamux-tab-strip-position, roamux-tab-strip-toggle-shortcut, roamux-tab-visit-nav.
#   kRoamuxSchemeAlias deliberately has no row (unchanged by roam-340).
